# --- Secrets: never commit API keys ---
# .env holds the real keys. There is no tracked template; the two names the app
# reads are GROQ_API_KEY and, for the retired Pinecone path, PINECONE_API_KEY.
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.key
groq_api_key.txt

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Local-only legacy stack (pre-Pinecone Flask + ChromaDB prototype) ---
# Kept on disk for reference; deliberately not part of this repo.
# Anchored with a leading slash so these only match at the repo root - an
# unanchored "app.py" would silently ignore any file of that name anywhere.
/app.py
/vector_db.py
/templates/
/db_chroma/

# --- Large local media not tracked in demo/ ---
/pawgpt_recording.mp4

# --- Private working notes, kept on disk but out of the repo ---
# Note-taking, interview preparation, and the deployment runbook. README.md is the
# only markdown the repo carries; it explains the project. The deployment steps are
# specific to one set of dashboards and accounts, so they stay local.
/INTERVIEW_NOTES.md
/ENGINEERING_NOTES.md
/DEPLOYMENT.md
/NOTES.md
/SCRATCH.md
/TODO.md

# --- Derived retrieval artifacts ---
# These ARE committed, deliberately, despite being generated files.
#
# The usual argument against is that they duplicate a source. The argument for is
# deployment: building the index means embedding 4,801 chunks on CPU, which took
# over ten minutes locally. Paying that inside a build timeout on every deploy, for
# a byte-identical result, is worse than carrying 12 MB in the repo.
#
# Regenerate with `python scripts/dedup_prose.py && python scripts/build_index.py`
# whenever the dataset, the chunking settings or the embedding model change, and
# commit the result alongside that change.
#   scripts/dedup_prose.py  -> data/breed_prose.json   (4.0 MB)
#   scripts/build_index.py  -> data/breed_index.npz    (7.9 MB)

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
